			"blurb": "Keycard Shell is a modular, fully open-source, air-gapped hardware wallet that signs via QR codes (ERC-4527). It has a built-in keypad, display, and camera, optional USB (can be turned off), and uses removable Keycards for secure key storage and backups. Keycard is a BIP-32 HD wallet running on JavaCard with EAL6+ secure element. Supports BIP-39 and SLIP-39 seed phrases.",
